{
  "description": "Stage 2 raises the finite verb to I, so the I⁰ head becomes a complex of V⁰ and the wrapped three-line label \"I⁰ [past, 3sg, definite conjugation]\" (a-infl), one row down beside Spec-VP. Stage 3 raises the subject Péter from Spec-VP to Spec-IP, and the attachments of stages 4 and 5 carry the later layout back over stage 2, where VP stands beside I⁰ at the place it takes once Spec-VP holds only the A-trace. Péter clears its own sister V′, so the held-slot pass left the plan alone, and in frames 24 to 26 the NP label overlapped the I⁰ label and the branch from VP to NP ran into it. VP now keeps the room its complete subject needs beside I⁰, from its construction on.",
